            <ArticleTitle>Strategy for optimal side-branch positioning of bioresorbable vascular scaffolds in dedicated 2-stent techniques: insights from optical coherence tomography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>298-300</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carrev.2014.01.015</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1553-8389(14)00046-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a left anterior descending artery/diagonal branch bifurcation successfully treated with a dedicated 2-stent technique utilizing bioresorbable vascular scaffolds, where the bifurcation angle did not strictly allow a T-stenting approach. We also propose a strategy to avoid or reduce scaffold overlap in the main branch, especially important in view of the bulkier size of these novel devices.</AbstractText>
